    {
      "id": "18401549692086118",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-12T13:56:53+01:00",
      "caption": "Much needed reset.\n\nOnly been to a handful of chill hikes like Bamford Edge, Rivelin Valley, and Arthur’s Seat, which were all under 300m of a climb. But nothing compared to hiking the base of the Matterhorn in Cervinia (more or less a 1,000m climb at just under 3,000m altitude). Despite being the slowest in the group, not bad for someone with a torn ACL (didn’t even buckle once) and hiking in AF1s!\n\nExperiences like this remind me how much of what goes on in our day-to-day lives doesn’t even matter. But you gotta play the game. Once I’m UP, I’m defo gonna disappear off into nature and live the rest of my life painting. Until then, I got a brand to build…\n\nBuilding @pioneersofgreatness\n\nGreatest,\nGALANA©CI",
