    {
      "id": "18103096396995066",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-13T03:43:57+01:00",
      "caption": "There’s no expiration date on ideas. Execute in da long run.\n\nProud of this one. First ever trousers I’ve designed from start to finish. From ideation, pattern drafting/cutting, prototyping, through to sampling.\n\nBut the job’s not done. I’ve only made two samples so far (one back in November 2025 and this one), as well as four prototypes.\n\nSo there’s still further refinement to be done:\n\n* slight tightness around the crotch area\n* fabric pooling beneath the glutes\n* further construction issues to resolve\n\n…But overall, the fit is there.\n\nCan’t emphasise enough how important it is to execute an idea and improve it later. And this right here is a testament to that.\n\nBack then, the best way I could bring an idea to life was through sketching, so that’s exactly what I did.\n\nBuilding @pioneersofgreatness\n\nGreatest,\nGALANA©CI",
